Subject: [PATCH] agent: a Topology Query is answered while a radio is in WSC once another radio is configured; a first onboarding waits as before

The agent answers a 1905 Topology Query only when every radio em of the queried AL MAC has
reached onewifi_bssconfig_ind (0003 skips the disabled ones). One radio redoing WSC, for every
Renew's window or a lost M2, therefore silenced the whole agent: no Topology Response, so the
controller saw it silent, and after 180 s retired an agent whose other radios were up.

With at least one radio configured, the response now goes out with the configured radios. A radio
still in WSC is not waited for and not marked topo_synchronized after the send (as 0003 does for a
disabled one); it is logged once per state, not once per query. The AP Operational BSS TLV still
lists it as it stands, so the controller's rule that retires a radio left out of three responses
in a row does not fire. On a first onboarding, no radio configured yet, the agent waits as before.
---
diff --git a/inc/em_configuration.h b/inc/em_configuration.h
index 882a9aa2..29ad2d11 100644
--- a/inc/em_configuration.h
+++ b/inc/em_configuration.h
@@ -1722,7 +1722,19 @@ public:
 	 * @note Ensure that the agent is initialized before calling this function.
 	 */
 	void process_agent_state();
-    
+
+	/* A Topology Query answered while this radio is in WSC: true when its state differs from the
+	 * one last logged for it, so the line comes once per state, not once per query. */
+	bool note_topo_query_wait(em_state_t state)
+	{
+		if (m_topo_query_wait_logged == static_cast<int>(state)) {
+			return false;
+		}
+		m_topo_query_wait_logged = static_cast<int>(state);
+		return true;
+	}
+	int m_topo_query_wait_logged = -1;
+
 	/**!
 	 * @brief Processes the control state.
 	 *
